    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10134" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">confirmātor</span></b> ,
		ōris, m.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>he who confirms</i> or <i>establishes a
			thing;</i> hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			Pecuniae, <i>a surety, security</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Clu.
				26, 72</span></i>: venditionis, Jul. Epit. Nov. c. 3, §
			10.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sententiae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lact. 1, 2 <i>init.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">erroris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Marc. 4, 36</span></i>
			.</div>
